# React Enterprise Standards

## Component Design
- Prefer functional components with hooks (avoid class components)
- Use 'use client' directive only when absolutely necessary
- Implement error boundaries for component failures
- Use React.memo() for expensive components
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks

## State Management
- Use React Query for server state (caching, refetching)
- Use Zustand or Redux Toolkit for global client state
- Keep components as stateless as possible
- Implement optimistic updates for better UX

## Performance
- Lazy load routes using React.lazy()
- Use virtualization for long lists (@tanstack/react-virtual)
- Implement debouncing for search inputs
- Bundle analyze and optimize chunks

## TypeScript
- Use strict mode and explicit types
- Export interfaces/types from shared file
- Use discriminated unions for state variations
- No 'any' - use 'unknown' and type guards

## Testing
- Test components with React Testing Library
- Test custom hooks with renderHook
- Integration tests for critical user flows
- Use MSW (Mock Service Worker) for API mocking
